# DOX — Runtime Adapter (compact)

> Installed skills load this compact kernel; full authoring material lives in
> `references/`, `examples/`, and the source `SKILL.md`. Calling the full
> protocol adds `~120` words of active surface, not thousands.

# DOX — Runtime Capsule

Documentation contract chain. Load before editing any file inside a
DOX-enabled project; closeout after the edit only when durable contracts
changed.

## Load
- Read the scoped AGENTS.md chain (root to target). A contract that applies
  to the edit target is binding: acknowledge it before editing.
- Missing/dir-adjacent contracts do not expand task scope.

## Closeout (only when durable contracts changed)
- Update AGENTS.md only for durable project contracts, ownership, scope,
  workflow, permissions, recurring rules, or child index structure.
- One-off FLOW tradeoffs stay in ANCHOR unless they establish a durable
  rule. Never create FLOW_ISSUES.md unless the user asks.

## Signals
contract_packet, closeout_packet

Emit in the canonical envelope only (shared/signal.schema.json); never
compute SISPIS scoring here.
